      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the structure. The original test has two issues:\n1. Wrapping single strings in arrays (`new String[] { \"Kobwick\" }`) just to call `encodeAll` adds unnecessary noise\n2. There's dead code: `assertEncodings` and `fullNysiis` are defined but never used\n\nI'll improve understandability by removing the dead code, eliminating the single-element array boilerplate, and adding comments explaining which NYSIIS branch each case targets.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the dead code (`fullNysiis` field and `assertEncodings` helper), eliminates the single-element array boilerplate in favor of direct `assertEquals` calls, and adds inline comments explaining which NYSIIS branch each test case exercises."
